12. Install Python and create a virtual environment
Purpose: Python will be used for AI application logic, API integration, Lambda functions, and Pinecone SDK exercises. Follow the trainer's specified version if one is provided.
Download and install a current Python 3 release compatible with the course. On Windows, enable Add Python to PATH if the installer offers it.
Open a new terminal and check Python and pip versions.
In your project folder, create a virtual environment named .venv.
Activate the environment using the command for your shell below.
python --version
python -m pip --version
python -m venv .venv

# Windows PowerShell
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

# Windows Git Bash
source .venv/Scripts/activate

# macOS/Linux
source .venv/bin/activate
python -m pip install --upgrade pip
python -c "print(\"Python environment is ready\")"
Verification test: Python and pip versions print, and the final command prints Python environment is ready. On some systems, use python3 instead of python.
Python downloads: https://www.python.org/downloads/
