16. Secrets and repository hygiene
Purpose: prevent accidental credential leaks that could expose cloud resources or create unexpected charges.
Create a .gitignore file in each project with at least these entries:
.venv/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.aws-sam/
☐ Use .env.example for placeholder names only, never real keys or passwords.
☐ Never commit AWS credentials, Pinecone API keys, passwords, tokens, private keys, or real customer data.
☐ Do not print secrets in logs or share screenshots that show credentials.
☐ If a key is exposed, revoke/rotate it immediately. Deleting the line in a later commit is not enough.
